    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0155" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 885.73/77</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-10T16:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My April 2, 11 a.m., and April 10, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d48-f1"/> In the
                    same conversation referred to in the last telegram the Uruguayan Minister
                    informed me that he had asked for an audience with the President of Argentina
                    before he left for Uruguay this evening, and he has stated to me that he would
                    urge upon him the importance of the granting of the Central &amp; South American
                    Telegraph Co.’s petition for permission to lay cable from Argentina to
                    Montevideo, informing him of the interest the Uruguayan Government had in the
                    matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
